  "excerpt": "This Christmas QEI celebrates its many international partnerships, which support sight-saving research for all Australians.",
  "body_html": "<p>This Christmas, in a year marked by conflict in many parts of the world, the Queensland Eye Institute celebrates its international colleagues, who support its research, education and clinical care.<br/>\nThese partnerships are important for sharing expertise from around the world. They ensure QEI can deliver state of the art eye care to people here in Queensland and our region.</p>\n<p>Breakthroughs in treating eye conditions like glaucoma and macular degeneration rarely happen in one laboratory. They take a team effort, and a sharing of information, skills and ideas. QEI’s involvement in shared projects ensures all Queenslanders will benefit from scientific breakthroughs when they happen, wherever that might be.</p>\n<p>All QEI clinicians have trained at world renowned eye centres overseas. They continue to draw on those relationships for the benefit of Queensland’s future eye health specialists and patients.</p>\n<p>QEI’s clinical trials for new therapies are all part of international efforts to prevent blindness and restore sight.</p>\n<p>As 2023 draws to a close, the Queensland Eye Institute Foundation extends sincere thanks to donors for their generosity and hopes for continued support. Donations to the Queensland Eye Institute Foundation form part of a global effort to combat eye disease, a worthy battle for the benefit of all Australians.</p>\n<h2>Science knows no borders</h2>\n<p>Professor Graham Holder from the National University of Singapore, previously from Moorfields Eye Hospital (London), visited the Queensland Eye Institute twice in 2023. Prof Holder spent time with Dr Sanket Vakil, QEI’s Visual Electrophysiologist and Clinical Researcher. He also delivered lectures to local ophthalmic trainees and shared his expertise with Queensland’s retinal specialists. The world leader came to Brisbane at the invitation of QEI’s Assoc Professor Anthony Kwan, who did his advanced training with Prof Holder in London.</p>\n<figure aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-4907\" class=\"wp-caption alignnone\" id=\"attachment_4907\" style=\"width: 1777px\"><img alt=\"Two men are seated at a desk with a computer on it. One man is wearing blue medical scrubs with the QEI logo on the shirt. The other man, who is older with a white beard, wears business clothes and has his hand on the computer mouse.\" class=\"wp-image-4907 size-full\" decoding=\"async\" fetchpriority=\"high\" height=\"1333\" id=\"longdesc-return-4907\" longdesc=\"https://qei.org.au?longdesc=4907&amp;referrer=4894\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1777px) 100vw, 1777px\" src=\"../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/QEDIC_ProfHolder-1.jpg\" srcset=\"../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/QEDIC_ProfHolder-1.jpg 1777w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/QEDIC_ProfHolder-1-300x225.jpg 300w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/QEDIC_ProfHolder-1-1024x768.jpg 1024w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/QEDIC_ProfHolder-1-768x576.jpg 768w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/QEDIC_ProfHolder-1-1536x1152.jpg 1536w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/QEDIC_ProfHolder-1-1430x1073.jpg 1430w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/QEDIC_ProfHolder-1-800x600.jpg 800w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/QEDIC_ProfHolder-1-400x300.jpg 400w\" tabindex=\"-1\" width=\"1777\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-caption-text\" id=\"caption-attachment-4907\">Professor Holder (R) is pictured with Dr Sanket Vakil, QEI’s Visual Electrophysiologist and Clinical Researcher</figcaption></figure>\n<p>QEI’s Executive Director and CEO, Prof. Mark Radford, travelled to Kuala Lumpur for the first in-person meeting of the Asia-Pacific Academy of Ophthalmology since the pandemic. With a theme of “Reconnect and Collaborate”, the congress brought together more than 4000 delegates from 78 countries to discuss the latest developments in eye research and clinical care.</p>\n<figure aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-4904\" class=\"wp-caption alignnone\" id=\"attachment_4904\" style=\"width: 2571px\"><img alt=\"A group of people, three women and two men, stand side-by-side in a conference room. They are in business clothes and have lanyards around their necks. They appear to be of Asian and Pacific Island heritage. \" class=\"wp-image-4904 size-full\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"1928\" id=\"longdesc-return-4904\" longdesc=\"https://qei.org.au?longdesc=4904&amp;referrer=4894\" sizes=\"(max-width: 2571px) 100vw, 2571px\" src=\"../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Prof-Radford-with-Asia-Pacific-colleagues.jpg\" srcset=\"../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Prof-Radford-with-Asia-Pacific-colleagues.jpg 2571w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Prof-Radford-with-Asia-Pacific-colleagues-300x225.jpg 300w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Prof-Radford-with-Asia-Pacific-colleagues-1024x768.jpg 1024w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Prof-Radford-with-Asia-Pacific-colleagues-768x576.jpg 768w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Prof-Radford-with-Asia-Pacific-colleagues-1536x1152.jpg 1536w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Prof-Radford-with-Asia-Pacific-colleagues-2048x1536.jpg 2048w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Prof-Radford-with-Asia-Pacific-colleagues-1430x1072.jpg 1430w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Prof-Radford-with-Asia-Pacific-colleagues-800x600.jpg 800w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Prof-Radford-with-Asia-Pacific-colleagues-400x300.jpg 400w\" tabindex=\"-1\" width=\"2571\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-caption-text\" id=\"caption-attachment-4904\">QEI’s Prof Mark Radford with Asia Pacific colleagues</figcaption></figure>\n<p>QEI’s Dr Alexandra Manta (R) shared her oculoplastic expertise with Romanian colleagues, demonstrating advanced surgical techniques to the research team. Dr Manta taught Asst Prof Florina Vultur to perform tarsal plate harvesting, supporting our joint research projects investigating human tissue and its role in novel therapeutic strategies.</p>\n<figure aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-4902\" class=\"wp-caption alignnone\" id=\"attachment_4902\" style=\"width: 768px\"><img alt=\"Two women in blue surgical gowns and gloves, wearing paper hair covers and disposable masks, lowered to show their faces, stand side by side in a room with apricot coloured walls. Beside them is a stainless steel trolley holding surgical equipment.\" class=\"wp-image-4902 size-full\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"576\" id=\"longdesc-return-4902\" longdesc=\"https://qei.org.au?longdesc=4902&amp;referrer=4894\" sizes=\"(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 768px\" src=\"../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Dr-Florina-Vultur-and-Dr-Alexandra-Manta.jpg\" srcset=\"../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Dr-Florina-Vultur-and-Dr-Alexandra-Manta.jpg 768w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Dr-Florina-Vultur-and-Dr-Alexandra-Manta-300x225.jpg 300w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Dr-Florina-Vultur-and-Dr-Alexandra-Manta-400x300.jpg 400w\" tabindex=\"-1\" width=\"768\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-caption-text\" id=\"caption-attachment-4902\">L-R Dr Florina Vultur and Dr Alexandra Manta</figcaption></figure>\n<p>QEI hosted Dr Rob Henderson of Great Ormond Street Hospital and Moorfields Eye Hospital in the United Kingdom. Dr Henderson spoke to Queensland ophthalmology trainees about his work on paediatric retinal gene therapy at the invitation of QEI’s Assoc Prof Anthony Kwan.</p>\n<figure aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-4903\" class=\"wp-caption alignnone\" id=\"attachment_4903\" style=\"width: 640px\"><img alt=\"A large group of people sit in a lecture theatre with their backs to the camera. They are looking at a projection on a large screen at the front of the room. Beside the screen two men stand at a lectern.\" class=\"wp-image-4903 size-full\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"480\" id=\"longdesc-return-4903\" loading=\"lazy\" longdesc=\"https://qei.org.au?longdesc=4903&amp;referrer=4894\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px\" src=\"../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Dr-Rob-Henderson-visit-2023.jpg\" srcset=\"../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Dr-Rob-Henderson-visit-2023.jpg 640w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Dr-Rob-Henderson-visit-2023-300x225.jpg 300w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Dr-Rob-Henderson-visit-2023-400x300.jpg 400w\" tabindex=\"-1\" width=\"640\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-caption-text\" id=\"caption-attachment-4903\">Dr Rob Henderson (L) and QEI’s Assoc Prof Anthony Kwan address Queensland trainees</figcaption></figure>\n<p>QEI’s Dr David Gunn shared his expertise in CAIRS (Corneal Allogenic Intrastromal Ring Segment) surgery at the European Society of Cataract and Refractive Surgeons meeting in Vienna. Under Dr Gunn’s leadership, QEI’s cornea team pioneered the first CAIRS surgery in Australia to treat keratoconus, a condition suffered by one in 84 Australians.</p>\n<figure aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-4901\" class=\"wp-caption alignnone\" id=\"attachment_4901\" style=\"width: 930px\"><img alt=\"Dr David Gunn stands on a stage behind a lectern, speaking into a microphone, addressing an audience in an auditorium. There is a desk on the stage with three people seated behind it. On the wall behind the stage is a large screen with a projection of a slide which reads “FEMTO-CUT CAIRS – ASYMMETRIC SEGMENTS AND FUTURE DEVELOPMENTS”\" class=\"wp-image-4901 size-full\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"661\" id=\"longdesc-return-4901\" loading=\"lazy\" longdesc=\"https://qei.org.au?longdesc=4901&amp;referrer=4894\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 930px) 100vw, 930px\" src=\"../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Dr-David-Gunn.jpeg.jpg\" srcset=\"../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Dr-David-Gunn.jpeg.jpg 930w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Dr-David-Gunn.jpeg-300x213.jpg 300w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Dr-David-Gunn.jpeg-768x546.jpg 768w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Dr-David-Gunn.jpeg-800x569.jpg 800w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Dr-David-Gunn.jpeg-400x284.jpg 400w\" tabindex=\"-1\" width=\"930\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-caption-text\" id=\"caption-attachment-4901\">Dr David Gunn presenting his research to the European Society of Cataract and Refractive Surgeons</figcaption></figure>\n<p>QEI’s Professors Mark Radford and Traian Chirila travelled to Romania to review progress on research projects at the University of Medicine, Pharmacy, Science and Technology “G.E. Palade” of Târgu Mureș (UMFST). The visit by QEI researchers further strengthened the relationship between USMFT and QEI and allowed the multi-disciplinary research team to plan its next steps.</p>\n<figure aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-4906\" class=\"wp-caption alignnone\" id=\"attachment_4906\" style=\"width: 1474px\"><img alt=\"Three men and a woman in casual clothes stand side-by-side on a cobblestone street in front of an old building. The building has large red doors, stone foundations and yellow painted rendered walls. A sign on the building says “Facultatea de medicina” \" class=\"wp-image-4906 size-full\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"1106\" id=\"longdesc-return-4906\" loading=\"lazy\" longdesc=\"https://qei.org.au?longdesc=4906&amp;referrer=4894\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1474px) 100vw, 1474px\" src=\"../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Romania-visit-Trian-Mark-and-Alexandra-at-medical-school.jpg\" srcset=\"../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Romania-visit-Trian-Mark-and-Alexandra-at-medical-school.jpg 1474w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Romania-visit-Trian-Mark-and-Alexandra-at-medical-school-300x225.jpg 300w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Romania-visit-Trian-Mark-and-Alexandra-at-medical-school-1024x768.jpg 1024w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Romania-visit-Trian-Mark-and-Alexandra-at-medical-school-768x576.jpg 768w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Romania-visit-Trian-Mark-and-Alexandra-at-medical-school-1430x1073.jpg 1430w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Romania-visit-Trian-Mark-and-Alexandra-at-medical-school-800x600.jpg 800w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Romania-visit-Trian-Mark-and-Alexandra-at-medical-school-400x300.jpg 400w\" tabindex=\"-1\" width=\"1474\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-caption-text\" id=\"caption-attachment-4906\">QEI’s Executive Director and CEO Prof Mark Radford, and Chief Scientist Prof Traian Chirila in Romania, accompanied by Dr Alexandra Manta</figcaption></figure>\n<h1>Supporting QEI Foundation</h1>\n<p>Queensland Eye Institute Foundation is Queensland’s largest independent academic research institute devoted to eye-related health and diseases. With your help, we can work towards new treatments and cures. At QEIF our mission is to reduce eye disease, improve eye health, and ultimately eliminate preventable blindness in the community. With no government funding, QEIF’s survival relies solely on the generosity of you and the community.</p>\n<h2>Donate here</h2>\n<div class=\"gf_browser_unknown gform_wrapper gform_legacy_markup_wrapper gform-theme--no-framework donate-foms_wrapper\" data-form-index=\"0\" data-form-theme=\"legacy\" id=\"gform_wrapper_9\">\n<div class=\"gform_heading\">\n<p class=\"gform_description\"></p>\n</div><form action=\"#\" aria-disabled=\"true\" autocomplete=\"off\" class=\"donate-foms\" data-formid=\"9\" data-original-action=\"index.html\" data-original-method=\"post\" data-qei-static-form=\"disabled\" enctype=\"multipart/form-data\" id=\"gform_9\" method=\"get\" novalidate=\"novalidate\" onsubmit=\"return false\">\n<div class=\"gform-body gform_body\"><ul class=\"gform_fields top_label form_sublabel_below description_below validation_below\" id=\"gform_fields_9\"><li class=\"gfield gfield--type-radio gfield--type-choice donation-tabs hide-label gfield_contains_required field_sublabel_below gfield--no-description field_description_below field_validation_below gfield_visibility_visible\" id=\"field_9_1\"><label class=\"gfield_label gform-field-label\">Donate types<span class=\"gfield_required\"><span class=\"gfield_required gfield_required_asterisk\">*</span></span></label><div class=\"ginput_container ginput_container_radio\"><ul class=\"gfield_radio\" id=\"input_9_1\">\n<li class=\"gchoice gchoice_9_1_0\">\n<input aria-disabled=\"true\